id: pm-qal1uw
title: Keep omitted SDK read options as precise first-page results
description: "PR1529 CodeRabbit inline4333511118 identifies an ergonomic refinement in InitialReadOptions: it imports the full ReadOptions shape, so a no-argument list context or search call remains omission-aware while an explicit empty object uses the first-page type. The conservative no-argument behavior already existed through the indexed ListOptions default; align omitted options with explicit empty options without changing runtime serialization. Explicit budgets sessions output cursors optional producer cursors and generic records must retain their existing narrowing requirements."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: review-feedback,sdk,types
created_at: "2026-10-21T06:11:30.169Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T06:23:56.030Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T06:23:54.728Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T06:23:54.728Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: No-argument client and standalone list context search calls expose first-page fields directly; empty-object calls match omitted calls; explicit budget session output-cursor union and optional producer-cursor calls retain omission or metadata narrowing; independent source and packed declaration cases fail before and pass after the refinement; SDK snapshot docs and package-generated changelog remain current
parent: pm-srns
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: Use an empty-key default for all client and standalone list context search read generics. Explicit ReadOptions constraints preserve budget session output-cursor union and producer metadata narrowing. Document the precise omitted and empty-object behavior and regenerate the public surface snapshot.
expected_result: No-argument SDK reads match explicit empty options while all explicit output-control and producer continuation safety contracts remain enforced in source and packed declarations.
actual_result: Independent before consumer fails TS2322 for no-argument ListResult assignments. Final PM-linked suite passes all four TypeScript configurations and 3 focused integration tests including actual npm tarball declaration compilation and Node/Bun journeys. Focused ESLint docs links SDK snapshot and docstring quality pass; final revised-head hosted admission remains required before merge.
