comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T06:11:30.169Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: full all-status lineage and fresh omitted argument default SDK and no argument first page searches plus open/in-progress inventories found no exact active refinement. The original producer and union fixes are completed in the current unmerged PR and remain closed. This new narrow review task preserves their delivered behavior and records the distinction between a precision improvement and a runtime regression. Review: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1529#discussion_r4333511118"
  "2026-10-21T06:14:05.110Z","harness:codex","Independent before proof through the current built public SDK: no-argument client.list() and standalone list() fail assignment to Promise<ListResult>, while an explicit empty object passes. The source change uses an empty-key generic default rather than importing optional output controls. Positive fixtures cover all six client/standalone read forms; existing negative cases continue to protect explicit budgets, sessions, output cursors, unions and producer metadata."
  "2026-10-21T06:23:32.622Z","harness:codex","Validation: the PM-linked suite passed all four TypeScript configurations and both focused integration files (3 tests), including declaration compilation through the actual npm tarball plus Node and Bun continuation journeys. Independent before fixture rejects the no-argument ListResult assignments with TS2322; after the empty-key generic default those six client/standalone declarations pass while all existing explicit-control negative assertions remain required. Focused ESLint, packaged docs links, SDK snapshot check and docstring quality pass. The prior full source coverage and initial PR required checks are green; the new pushed revision will require fresh exact-head CI admission."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T06:23:31.924Z","harness:codex","Generic default options are observable API behavior: omit keys entirely for omitted arguments rather than importing optional budget or cursor keys from broad option interfaces. Compile no-argument, empty-object, optional and union options through the public packed SDK to preserve both ergonomics and truthful narrowing."
